WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.661 --> 00:00:26.560
In the previous video, we started the 
renovation of our German yellow van.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.280
We want to transform it into a comfortable,
and long lasting living space.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.800
We leveled it, and ripped it apart.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.360
We started planning
and designing the new interior.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.360
Dig the trench to bring electricity
and change the door.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.280
Now, we are going to finish the work.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.440
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.880
So, here we are, back in the van.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.000
Last, night we took out the roof.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.520
Now, we have some sort of a cabriolet.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.920
We cover it with a tarp just in case
the rain comes, to not ruin all of our work.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.074
Now, the next step would be
 to put in the roof, insulate the whole van...

00:00:59.074 --> 00:01:03.800
And, start with the fun part, which is the details
 the furniture, and finish up the space.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.680
So, the first thing needed is to make
the frame for the interior and the roof.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.520
We're going to start
by cutting the wooden beams.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.280
And now, the beams of the frame are finished!

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.320
As you can see, the fiberglass is out.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.320
So, we're going to start roofing.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:01.039
First, we add some of the wall studs
on top of the van to all the rafters.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.080
And now, we can put the rafters on.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:57.000
So, this is the old driver's seat.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.654
And, because we want to add a table
over there for working...

00:05:00.654 --> 00:05:05.160
We want to turn the old seat 90 degrees, to face that way.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:09.640
So, that's why we are trying
to take the rail up and reangle the seat.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:14.480
And then, we find a lot of switches
around the cockpit.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:18.480
So, this is one of the switches
that used to connect the old battery.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:26.630
And, we think it is very interesting,
and we might be able to use it for the light of the van.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:08.218
It's easier if you can just
 move it like this, to I guess work?

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.794
Cool!

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:13.852
Next!

00:06:13.852 --> 00:06:15.583
Okay, as you can see, the framing is done!

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.800
Right now, we are going to start with insulation.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:20.360
We're going to use the same materials in the ruin.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:21.480
It's cork.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.480
So, yeah, let's go!

00:07:24.185 --> 00:07:29.185
Now that the walls are insulated, 
we need to get some wood to cover it.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.080
We got a call from the local sawmill.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:08:01.080
They just received a batch of old floor,
from a sport club of the town close by.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:07.329
So, it’s this kind of wood that used to be flooring
 for a basketball court, for futsal

00:08:07.329 --> 00:08:10.400
And, it's in very good state actually!

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:12.720
It still has the lines, as you can see.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:18.362
But, we thought this was a great opportunity for us to get!

00:08:18.362 --> 00:08:22.680
And, to see what we can do with it, to include it
in our renovation of the yellow van. 

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:08.120
We like this wood for several reasons.

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:12.066
It's reused, it's high quality, which would make it last longer.

00:09:12.066 --> 00:09:14.011
And, otherwise, no one would use it...

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:18.120
On top of it, we are also going
for the offcuts of this batch.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:22.960
This will definitely bring more challenge to the process,
but we like to reuse as much as we can.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:26.360
And if not us, then who?

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:29.720
Yeah, so, we got this pile of wood from the sawmill yesterday.

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:32.240
You can see there’s a lot of tracks, a lot of dirt...

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:37.240
So, the first step we need to do to reuse 
is to sand it and clean it.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:51.480
We sanded one side and on the other side,
we kept the original plastic layer.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.744
This is good for protecting the wood.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:15.240
With the roof boards in place, I made a small frame
where I'm going to put the cork in.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.280
Okay, so we're going to start isolating the roof.

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:45.680
We're going to use cork again!

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:48.640
And, after that, a metal sheet to make it waterproof.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.800
Okay, so, we finished putting the isolation on the roof.

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:41.412
We made a frame around the isolation

00:12:41.412 --> 00:12:45.240
Because, we're going to put a metal sheet over it,
and we're going to bend it over.

00:13:02.611 --> 00:13:04.313
- Move it a tiny bit.

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:17.548
Perfect!

00:13:45.199 --> 00:13:46.534
- You got it?

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:47.519
Yup!

00:13:47.519 --> 00:13:48.356
- Cool!

00:13:48.356 --> 00:13:50.000
Went well!

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:16.840
Okay, so, I'm using the wood that Kevin is sanding.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:20.400
It's wood from an old basketball court, from around here.

00:14:22.021 --> 00:14:25.490
Yeah, it's pretty tough to fit,
 because it's already been fit...

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:31.060
This is the second time we are putting it together,
so the joints are broken, and they don't fit very well...

00:14:31.060 --> 00:14:33.000
So, we have to hammer them down.

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:35.200
But, it's looking really nice!

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:38.480
And yes, reclaimed wood, and also white oak.

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:40.000
So, it's going to be beautiful!

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:03.320
Okay, so, we are making progress 
on the walls and on the floor.

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:09.993
But, before we are starting with this wall,
we are going to frame, like a little box here.

00:17:10.343 --> 00:17:12.350
So, we can run the wires through it.

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:18.605
And, then first, we are going to cover this box,
 with the same oak panels

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:22.155
And then, start on this wall...

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:42.480
So, we finished what we had to do to be able,
to finish the siding.

00:17:44.087 --> 00:17:49.511
We ran the cables through also, 
because now we're going to put two sockets on this side.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.689
Precious Plastic sockets!

00:17:51.689 --> 00:17:54.680
So yeah, socket time!

00:19:05.151 --> 00:19:09.353
Okay, so, we have this old switch 
of the battery system that was in the van...

00:19:09.703 --> 00:19:15.240
And, we want to use it to as the switch for the LED-lights, 
that we're going to put in the van.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:19.120
So, yeah, just try to fit it in, and see if it works!

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:50.268
We are connecting the switch,
 and checking if the net works.

00:19:50.268 --> 00:19:51.359
Or, if the switch works...

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:53.731
I already installed the transformer!

00:19:54.466 --> 00:20:00.080
Kevin wants to reuse this old light,
that was in the van as a reading light.

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:06.320
So, yeah, I'm going to run the wire for this thing here,
and then the wires for the LED strip.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:08.840
Okay!

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:10.080
Let’s check...

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.559
- Okay.

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:13.680
Yeah?

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:17.881
So, it wasn't as easy as we expected, was it Kevin?

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:21.502
- Yeah, it is!

00:20:21.502 --> 00:20:24.240
But, it works!

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:26.788
So, we are happy.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.840
Cool!

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:34.560
Okay, the electrics are in place.

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:36.880
Now, we can finish the walls.

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:53.120
- Is it Christmas, Jaime?

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.960
It’s Christmas, yeah...

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.440
So, most of the siding is done.

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:12.000
We are still missing the last pieces,
but we're waiting for the lights, because we want to put lights in it.

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:18.040
So, now, we are going to start making the bed,
 and the little sink area.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:08.924
I'm now trying to build a table here,
because we're turning this travel seat around.

00:22:08.924 --> 00:22:11.280
And, we try to use this place as an office.

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:15.120
So, we need a two level table here.

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:17.920
The lower part will be movable.

00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:23.613
It will slide out and slide in,
to be more flexible in this space.

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:56.000
So, this is now a snug office!

00:22:56.000 --> 00:23:00.920
And then, we are going to finish
all the little stuff, like the curtains...

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:05.320
Other details, things with the sewing machine,
 and with old fabric.

00:23:05.600 --> 00:23:08.600
And, so, this will be the sewing station for now.

00:23:38.630 --> 00:23:44.065
Okay, so, right now, I'm going to start cutting,
and preparing these old cedar boards.

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:49.480
We're going to make a little sink area,
and a wardrobe from it.

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:54.320
So, cutting, sanding, and then I will install it in the yellow van.

00:24:13.520 --> 00:24:15.640
So, the sink area is almost done.

00:24:15.640 --> 00:24:17.560
Now, we're going to try it!

00:24:21.306 --> 00:24:22.680
So, the shelves are almost done!

00:24:22.680 --> 00:24:25.680
And, now, we're going to go to the van, and try and fit it.

00:24:45.360 --> 00:24:46.680
Hello Kevin!

00:24:46.680 --> 00:24:48.640
- Hello!

00:25:11.812 --> 00:25:13.480
Everything fits!

00:25:13.600 --> 00:25:20.635
Now, the last part is to make a hole here,
 to fit the new sink.

00:26:04.120 --> 00:26:07.760
Okay, so, all the siding is done, finally.

00:26:08.240 --> 00:26:10.760
So, now, we're going to start sanding everything again.

00:26:10.760 --> 00:26:14.640
But, luckily, I have the best sander in the Kamp...

00:26:15.800 --> 00:26:16.595
Mariona!

00:26:16.595 --> 00:26:17.550
- Hello!

00:26:17.550 --> 00:26:18.855
Ready to get your hands dirty?

00:26:18.855 --> 00:26:20.175
- Yes, let’s go!

00:26:21.120 --> 00:26:22.680
Let's start sanding!

00:26:57.800 --> 00:27:00.315
So, everything is sanded!

00:27:00.315 --> 00:27:05.480
We vacuumed all of the dust out,
and now we're going to start oiling.

00:27:05.920 --> 00:27:11.000
We're going to use a thin coat of linseed oil, in the whole van.

00:27:11.360 --> 00:27:13.680
So, yeah, let’s start oiling.

00:27:57.240 --> 00:27:58.840
Okay, all of that is now done!

00:27:58.840 --> 00:28:02.125
Now, I'm putting LED strip on the edge of the wall.

00:28:02.335 --> 00:28:07.560
Which is this one, to try to mimic the effect 
of having light, coming through from the roof.

00:28:07.560 --> 00:28:08.460
Blue is red?

00:28:08.460 --> 00:28:10.560
- Blue is black!

00:28:10.920 --> 00:28:13.920
I am putting the solder...

00:28:14.920 --> 00:28:16.560
- And, I'm pretty happy he's doing it...

00:28:16.560 --> 00:28:18.600
I have fat fingers.

00:28:48.040 --> 00:28:49.440
It works!

00:28:50.966 --> 00:28:54.880
Okay, so, right now we are already
on the final steps of the build.

00:28:55.760 --> 00:29:03.360
We're going to be finishing up some details,
and Kevin is still finishing curtains and everything with fabric.

00:29:03.360 --> 00:29:09.840
I'm going to be installing the door lock, 
the door knob, wood trims around it...

00:29:09.920 --> 00:29:13.668
And, yeah, some little stuff that still has to be done.

00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:54.563
Let’s go in!

00:29:56.240 --> 00:30:00.000
So, this part is really transparent,
and everyone can see through.

00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:06.560
So, for this curtain, we choose some thick fabric,
like the jeans, to make a curtain to cover.

00:30:27.360 --> 00:30:30.480
With this white fabric, the light really goes through.

00:30:30.480 --> 00:30:32.400
So, we want to put it at a door.

00:30:32.400 --> 00:30:36.080
Now, I'm taking it apart really carefully...

00:31:59.880 --> 00:32:01.320
Do you know what this is, Mariona?

00:32:01.480 --> 00:32:03.360
- No, what is it, Jaime?

00:32:03.680 --> 00:32:05.160
It's the last piece.

00:32:05.160 --> 00:32:06.396
- No!

00:32:06.396 --> 00:32:08.160
Yeah!

00:32:23.640 --> 00:32:25.200
I'm done...

00:32:26.726 --> 00:32:28.840
Jaime, what is this piece here? 

00:32:28.840 --> 00:32:29.424
Is it not oiled?

00:32:29.424 --> 00:32:30.222
- This one?

00:32:30.782 --> 00:32:32.798
It’s the funny thing about filming...

00:32:32.800 --> 00:32:36.360
You put on a GoPro, and then you forget to oil it...

00:32:36.840 --> 00:32:38.520
So, yeah, we have to oil it again.

00:32:39.361 --> 00:32:41.400
But, it's just a little piece...

00:32:41.440 --> 00:32:42.655
Not that much...

00:32:42.655 --> 00:32:43.378
- Easy peasy?

00:32:44.360 --> 00:32:45.360
We’re close to finishing the van.

00:32:45.560 --> 00:32:48.560
Now, I'm putting the slats in place,
so we can put the mattress in.

00:33:11.840 --> 00:33:16.440
So, we already finished the bed,
and the mattress has arrived.

00:33:17.160 --> 00:33:18.240
So, we're going to put the mattress in.

00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:21.640
That's it!

00:33:40.200 --> 00:33:41.728
Fits good!

00:33:45.600 --> 00:33:49.520
In the meantime, I'm doing the sheets for 
the new bed, made out of old shirts.

00:33:50.400 --> 00:33:52.280
We like to give new life to material.

00:33:52.280 --> 00:33:55.280
So, we got this shirt from a second hand shop close by.

00:34:00.480 --> 00:34:02.324
Ready to sew!

00:34:07.320 --> 00:34:11.098
Around this height, or...?

00:34:11.098 --> 00:34:15.960
With the leftover pockets, I decided to make something
 next to the bed, to keep the gadgets organized.

00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:19.920
- What's that for, Kevin?

00:34:21.286 --> 00:34:24.320
This is for the phone to sleep in.

00:34:24.320 --> 00:34:26.160
- Hey, cool!

00:34:27.080 --> 00:34:30.080
I also installed a little rack to hang clothes.

00:34:33.480 --> 00:34:36.680
Okay, so, we finished the last pieces of furniture.

00:34:36.840 --> 00:34:40.720
So, now, the only thing that’s left is to oil them.

00:34:53.120 --> 00:34:56.000
I could oil like this all day.

00:34:56.000 --> 00:34:57.353
Comfy!

00:35:00.200 --> 00:35:02.040
This van will not drive anymore.

00:35:02.040 --> 00:35:03.800
So, I have a better place for this mirror!

00:35:25.341 --> 00:35:29.360
The old license plate could be a nice decoration!

00:35:32.040 --> 00:35:33.640
It's from Croatia!

00:35:37.760 --> 00:35:41.400
So, one of the things we found on the van is this dry frog.

00:35:41.400 --> 00:35:46.440
Which, Mattia found when he first got this van.

00:35:46.880 --> 00:35:54.301
When I found this van, I just also encountered 
this splashed frog and I kept it there ever since.

00:35:54.301 --> 00:35:57.360
As a sort of a sign of good luck!

00:35:57.800 --> 00:36:00.800
So, we are making a little frame for it!

00:36:32.080 --> 00:36:34.263
Okay, the van is finished!

00:36:34.800 --> 00:36:38.526
To give it a final touch, we put some woodchips around it.

00:36:43.945 --> 00:36:46.520
Okay, right now, the entrance of the van is a bit high...

00:36:46.520 --> 00:36:52.210
So, I just got this wood and I'm going 
to make two steps, to make the entrance more comfy.

00:37:51.600 --> 00:37:53.520
So, the van now is done!

00:37:53.520 --> 00:37:55.066
A nice house on wheels!

00:37:55.066 --> 00:37:59.520
Even though it's not going to drive anymore, 
for our set up at Basekamp, it’s a perfect fit.

00:37:59.520 --> 00:38:03.600
Now that we repaired the roof, 
it can last many more years in perfect state.

00:38:04.680 --> 00:38:06.304
We love the look of the interior!

00:38:06.304 --> 00:38:11.560
All wood, properly insulated with natural cork, 
with night lights and a lot of details.

00:38:12.400 --> 00:38:16.320
It will be a nice place to live for a
longer period of time, even during winter.

00:38:16.640 --> 00:38:20.600
In the next video, we will show you what happens
 in Project Kamp behind the scenes,

00:38:20.915 --> 00:38:22.795
Something you don't see in the normal updates!

00:38:23.080 --> 00:38:25.920
If you want to see it now, you can support us on Patreon!

00:38:25.920 --> 00:38:28.200
You can find the link in the description of the video.

00:38:28.200 --> 00:38:30.080
Click there and see what happens.

00:38:30.080 --> 00:38:33.600
If not, you can always subscribe,
and help us with the algorithm.

00:38:34.640 --> 00:38:36.720
Thanks for watching and you in the next update!

